gs":[{"technique_id":"T1685.002","name":"Disable or Modify Cloud Log","parent":"Disable or Modify Tools","tactics":["Defense Impairment"],"behavior":"payload.exe spawned auditpol.exe to disable audit categories (DS Access, Account Logon), remove user auditing, and clear the audit log via auditpol /clear /y, while modifying LSA registry keys to disable audit settings.","slot":0,"reasoning":"The operator used auditpol.exe to disable audit categories (DS Access, Account Logon), clear the audit log, and modify LSA registry keys to suppress audit settings. This is direct tampering with Windows audit policy to impair detection capabilities, which is the core objective of disabling Windows audit logging rather than clearing event logs after the fact.","evidence":[{"event_id":"E021","field":"CommandLine","quote":"auditpol.exe /set /user:pedro /category:\"DS Access\" /success:disable","ok":true},{"event_id":"E037","field":"CommandLine","quote":"auditpol.exe /clear /y","ok":true},{"event_id":"E039","field":"TargetObject","quote":"HKLM\\System\\CurrentControlSet\\Control\\Lsa\\CrashOnAuditFail","ok":true}],"attempts":1},{"technique_id":"T1654","name":"Log Enumeration","parent":null,"tactics":["Discovery"],"behavior":"PowerShell executed Get-WinEvent commands to query and exfiltrate Security and Application event logs with time-based filtering before the logs were cleared.","slot":1,"reasoning":"The operator used Get-WinEvent with time-based FilterXPath parameters to query both Security and Application event logs, which is log enumeration to discover potentially valuable audit data. This is discovery activity (querying logs for information), not defense evasion (clearing logs), so T1654 is the primary objective rather than T1685.005.","evidence":[{"event_id":"E049","field":"Payload","quote":"CommandInvocation(Get-WinEvent): \"Get-WinEvent\" ParameterBinding(Get-WinEvent): name=\"LogName\"; value=\"Application\"","ok":true},{"event_id":"E050","field":"Payload","quote":"CommandIn